# Test/security dependency contract — Phase 8.7-D.1 (source updated for
# Phase 8.7-D.1-CORRECTION-3, Finding E).
#
# SOURCE OF TRUTH for what EVERY Python test/security CI job installs.  The
# compiled, fully-transitive, hash-pinned lock is `requirements-test.txt`
# (generated — do not edit by hand):
#
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes --strip-extras \
#       -o requirements-test.txt requirements-test.in
#
# CI installs ONLY this file per Python job, with `pip install
# --require-hashes`.  The runtime Dockerfiles install `requirements-runtime.txt`.
#
# SHARED-VERSION CONTRACT: the first block below pins EXACTLY the versions
# that `requirements-runtime.txt` carries for every package both
# environments need (fastapi/starlette/anyio/pydantic/redis/requests/PyJWT).
# The dependency-parity guard (mutation M29) fails CI if the two locks ever
# disagree on any of them — the container and the test suite run on one
# compatible dependency set, never on two drifting ones.
#
# Rationale for the pinned generation: see requirements-runtime.in (last
# pre-starlette-1.0 generation; anyio 4.12.1 predates the BlockingPortal
# deprecation; verified warning-free by the full security suite).

# --- shared runtime set (MUST match requirements-runtime.txt versions) ---
fastapi==0.128.8
starlette==0.52.1
anyio==4.12.1
pydantic==2.14.1
redis==8.1.0
requests==2.34.2
PyJWT==2.15.1

# --- test/security-only dependencies ---
httpx==0.28.1
pytest==9.1.1
pyyaml==6.0.3
